/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  THE MULTIBED CONVERTER -- ONE SECTOR, ONE PRESSURE VESSEL (DEV.md 4c C69).

  Three adiabatic catalyst beds with an interbed cooler after each of the
  first two.  The flowsheet still computes FIVE blocks -- each bed and each
  cooler is a calculation of its own -- but they are built as ONE piece of
  equipment: the beds sit in a basket inside a single pressure shell, with
  the interbed exchange inside the same shell.  That is a fact about the
  EQUIPMENT, so it is said where the equipment is sized:
  system/postDict's `converterShell` entry names this sector, stacks its
  members' geometries into one shell at the loop's design pressure, and the
  beds' own shells become internal baskets that are not priced twice.

  WHERE THE ARRANGEMENT WAS READ (2026-10-12), and what was not:
    * The M. W. Kellogg Company, "Ammonia synthesis converter", EP 0 254 936
      A2 (1988), read on the EPO publication server: "the vertical converter
      is contained within cylindrical pressure shell 1", three axial-flow
      catalyst beds "within the cylindrical inner shell", and interbed
      cooling "supplied entirely by the single indirect heat exchanger"
      inside it -- ONE interbed exchanger, not two.
    * Topsoe, "Ammonia converter baskets S-300" (product page, read): three
      catalyst beds, radial flow, a BASKET installed in a pressure shell, in
      one version with an integral feed-effluent exchanger after the third
      bed.  The page does not describe its interbed exchangers.
  Neither source describes TWO interbed coolers raising steam, as these two
  do; that arrangement is the base case's, and the one-shell grouping is the
  sources' general construction applied to it.

  The stream names are the plant's, unchanged: the sector's inlet is the
  FEHE's preheated feed, its outlet the hot effluent the FEHE cools.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    Bed1
    InterbedCooler1
    Bed2
    InterbedCooler2
    Bed3
);

connections
{
    PreheatedFeed { to Bed1/Feed; }
    Bed1Out       { from Bed1/Out;             to InterbedCooler1/Feed; }
    Bed2Feed      { from InterbedCooler1/Out;  to Bed2/Feed; }
    Bed2Out       { from Bed2/Out;             to InterbedCooler2/Feed; }
    Bed3Feed      { from InterbedCooler2/Out;  to Bed3/Feed; }
    HotEffluent   { from Bed3/Out; }
}
